    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">A <strong>perfect square factor</strong> is a number that is a square of a whole number, such as 4, 9, 16, 25, and so on. We use perfect square factors to simplify surds by writing the number under the root as a product of a perfect square and another number.</p>",
